  "decision": "Held the $5K estimate at 61% and the $10K estimate at 31%. The Bank of Japan's 25-basis-point hike to 1.25%, following the Federal Reserve's increase, confirms synchronized global tightening and keeps cyclical macro scores at the floor. ETH nevertheless held near $2.47K, network staking increased to 43.27M ETH, and Ethereum's DeFi and tokenized-asset footprint remained large. Three-session ETF outflows reached $405.4M, but cumulative inflows remained about $13.14B and traditional-finance adoption continued through S&P Global's OpenZeppelin acquisition agreement. The SEC's five-year tokenized-securities exemption provides a concrete but narrow operating path after CLARITY failed, so regulation improves modestly without leaving red. Direct L1 economics remain small relative to application activity and non-Ethereum settlement competition preserves the explicit $10K value-capture penalty. No catalyst crossed a color threshold."
